# Repos the VM suite needs checked out BESIDE it on the CI venue.
#
# Declaring a sibling here is what makes its cross-repo guards actually run. An
# UNdeclared sibling is not a neutral omission: every guard written against it
# resolves with existsSync, calls this.skip(), and the gate still prints PASS,
# so the run reports green having exercised none of them. Measured 2026-08-12 on
# Linux (isolated-vm does not load on macOS), that gap was 19 tests: a venue
# carrying only documentation + indexer ran 901 passing / 19 pending where a full
# checkout runs 920 / 13. The undeclared pair was xchain-sdk and xchain-contracts,
# so lint-core parity and the contract-template lint parity had never run on the
# venue. See test/unit/sibling-coverage.test.js, which reports the surface this
# file leaves uncovered; the same gap applies to a sibling that is declared but
# missing.
#
# ci-dispatch.sh ships each of these at its origin/master (falling back to local
# HEAD) and REFUSES the push if one is not a checkout beside this repo, so a
# declared sibling can never be silently absent.

# The canonical XCALL constant map.
xchain-documentation
# XCALL constant parity and the consensus-params twin.
xchain-indexer
# XCALL constant parity and lint-core parity.
xchain-sdk
# Lint parity over every shipped contract source: <name>/<name>.js templates and
# patterns/*.js pattern sources (both discovered, not enumerated).
xchain-contracts
